      <div class="lph-faq">
        <details open><summary>Is Leapproof legit?</summary><div><p>Fair question. If you’ve bought “leak-proof” underwear off an ad before, you’ve probably been burned. Here’s what we put in writing: you get 30 nights to test them, and if they don’t hold, we refund your whole set and you keep the pairs. You pay once, with no subscription. Shipping is free. A real person answers every email at <a href="mailto:hello@leapproof.com">hello@leapproof.com</a>. Our <a href="/policies/refund-policy">refund</a> and <a href="/policies/shipping-policy">shipping</a> policies are linked at the bottom of every page.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How much can they hold?</summary><div><p>They’re made for lighter leaks: a few drops to a small splash on a sneeze, laugh or jump. If it’s more than that, these may not be enough on their own, and a pelvic floor physical therapist is worth a chat.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>I already own period underwear. Why these?</summary><div><p>Keep them for your period. These are for the sneeze, the laugh and the jump the rest of the month: plain black briefs from $9.90 a pair, so you can own a full week’s worth instead of one “just in case” pair. Sized by your hips (US 0–20), with 30 nights to test them.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Will they feel bulky or show under leggings?</summary><div><p>No pad, so nothing bulky. They’re cut like regular briefs with a soft, smooth waistband. Wear them under leggings, jeans or work pants.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How do I pick my size?</summary><div><p>Measure around the widest part of your hips and use the <a href="#sizes">size chart</a>. Your usual US size is listed next to each one. Between two sizes? Pick the smaller one.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Can I wear them to train or run?</summary><div><p>Yes, for training, a run or a big day out. They’re made for lighter leaks, so if you leak more at night, they may not be enough on their own.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Can I wear them on my period?</summary><div><p>They’re made for lighter leaks, not as period underwear. On your period, use what you normally use.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How do I wash them?</summary><div><p>1. Rinse them in cold water after you take them off.<br>2. Zip them into a mesh wash bag (the Wash Bag comes free with 5 or 10 pairs) and machine wash cold (86°F / 30°C max) on a gentle cycle.<br>3. Use a mild detergent with no fabric softener, or the Wash Sheets.<br>4. Hang them to dry. No dryer, no bleach, no ironing.</p><p>Heat and softener are hard on the lining. Skip both and your pairs are made to be worn and washed again and again.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Will they smell?</summary><div><p>Wash them after every wear, like any underwear, and follow the steps above. Skipping softener keeps the lining soaking up properly. We don’t claim they’re “antibacterial,” because we haven’t tested that.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Have they been lab tested?</summary><div><p>Not by a third-party lab yet. So we don’t claim things like “PFAS-free” or a number of milliliters. When we have lab results, we’ll post them here. What we can tell you: 95% regenerated fiber, 5% spandex.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Is this a subscription?</summary><div><p>No. You pay once for the set you pick. Nothing renews, and we never charge you again unless you say yes.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>When will they arrive?</summary><div><p>We pack your order in 1–3 business days, and most orders arrive about 6–10 days after you order. Shipping is free. With 10 pairs, the Wash Sheets come in a separate parcel and may arrive a few days apart.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>What if they don’t work or don’t fit?</summary><div><p>Doesn’t hold: email us within your 30 nights and we refund your whole set, processed within 3 business days. You keep the pairs. Wrong size? We’ll send your new size free. Nothing to send back. One Leak-Test claim per customer, one free size swap per order.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Do I have to take the quiz?</summary><div><p>No. If you know your size, <a href="#sets">pick a set</a> and choose your size at checkout. The quiz is the quickest way to get your size and the right number of pairs: about 2 minutes, and no email needed to see your match.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Who’s behind Leapproof?</summary><div><p>A small brand from Melbourne, Australia, started because women keep being told leaking is just part of life. Every email is answered by a real person: <a href="mailto:hello@leapproof.com">hello@leapproof.com</a>.</p></div></details>
